{"requirements":[{"id":"firewall-persistent","requirement":"A host firewall is enabled on node1 and remains effective after restart.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Firewalld was active and enabled before the restart. The acknowledged restart changed the boot ID, after which firewalld was again active and enabled with the intended policy present. Fixed lifecycle observations independently confirm the boot transition.","evidence_ids":["cmd-8c2c45e09b8e42f7","cmd-bb8229d990804b27","cmd-bd510384b5794022","cmd-1be15a8a8b344879","global:before_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity"]},{"id":"allow-ssh-8080","requirement":"The firewall permits inbound SSH and TCP port 8080.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Runtime and permanent firewalld queries returned yes for SSH and TCP/8080, and the active IPv4 and IPv6 rules explicitly accept ports 22 and 8080 on eth0. SSH was listening and reachable again after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-9da3ebc2888d42af","cmd-0e77f8327a7f44de","cmd-1be15a8a8b344879","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets"]},{"id":"reject-unrelated-inbound","requirement":"Unrelated inbound connections are rejected.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The active IPv4 and IPv6 INPUT paths assign eth0 to the public zone, allow the requested ports, and terminate unmatched inbound traffic with explicit REJECT rules. These rules remained after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-0e77f8327a7f44de","cmd-8c2c45e09b8e42f7","cmd-1be15a8a8b344879"]}],"confidence":0.94,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.97,"summary":"The firewall change and restart were necessary and tightly scoped, with no failed services or unexpected listener changes afterward. The only unnecessary retained mutation was /tmp/benchmark-reboot.log: cmd-bb8229d990804b27 created it while scheduling the required restart, but it was not removed and remained in the final snapshot. The failed discovery command and expected SSH timeout during reboot show no unwanted mutation.","evidence_ids":["cmd-bb8229d990804b27","cmd-719181f5ab5144ed","cmd-5cf7413466ff4330","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets"]},"overall_summary":"The required persistent firewall outcome is satisfied. Node1 allows SSH and TCP/8080, rejects unmatched inbound IPv4 and IPv6 traffic, and recovered with the same effective policy after a directly observed reboot. The mandatory restart protocol is complete for the single managed node: healthy pre-state, acknowledgement, changed boot identity, and recovered firewall and SSH state are all captured.","limitations":["No external connection probe directly attempted TCP/8080 or an unrelated port; the conclusion relies on direct inspection of the active kernel firewall rules and firewalld state.","Package-health checks timed out both before and after execution, so package consistency could not be independently assessed.","No application data or cluster state was identified in the single-node topology; restart recovery evidence therefore covers OS identity, services, listener state, and firewall policy."]}
